1:# Problem Map - organizer-fee-paid-checkbox-20261005
2:
3:## Problem statement
4:
5:In the organizer `Đăng ký & Vận động viên` tab the registration fee is shown as a
6:read-only status badge: a green tick when `participant.isPaid`, a grey cross when not.
7:An organizer who collects the fee in cash or by bank transfer has no way to record
8:it, so the roster cannot be finalised even though the money is in hand.
9:
10:The request: make that column a checkbox the organizer controls directly, with these
11:rules.
12:
13:| Action | Meaning | Money |
14:|---|---|---|
15:| Tick | "I have this person's fee" — a manual mark, used for cash/bank transfer | none moves |
16:| Untick, no system payment | undo a manual mark | no refund, nothing financial |
17:| Untick, system payment exists | return the money | creates a refund request |
18:
19:Unticking must warn first, because one of the two cases creates a refund.
20:
21:## Evidence
22:
23:| # | Evidence |
24:|---|---|
25:| E1 | `RegistrationTab.tsx:913-922` (before) rendered a green circle with `Check` when `participant.isPaid`, else a grey `X`. No control. |
26:| E2 | `tournament_participants.is_paid` is a denormalised boolean. The only normal writer is `transitionPayment` (`payments.repository.ts:355-361`) when a gateway payment completes. |
27:| E3 | `PATCH :id/participants/:participantId` (`tournaments.controller.ts:1568-1586`) accepts only `status`. No fee flag. |
28:| E4 | `TournamentParticipant.payment` is nullable (`types/tournament.ts:332-343`). A manual mark produces no payment row, so `payment == null` is exactly the "no system payment" case. |
29:| E5 | Refunds are two-phase. Request: `createPendingRefund` (`tournament-payment.repository.ts:199-246`) CAS-flips `refund_status` NULL to `PENDING_REFUND` and inserts one `payment_refunds` row. Settle: `POST /payments/admin/payments/:id/confirm-refund`, `@Roles(ADMIN)` only, needs a proof URL. No gateway reversal call exists anywhere. |
30:| E6 | `createPendingRefund` takes the amount as input, but every existing caller derives it from `calculateTournamentRefundQuote` (`utils/tournament-refund-policy.ts:40`). The amount is never caller-supplied. |
31:| E7 | `financial_ledger_entries.idempotency_key` is `notNull().unique()` (`payments.schema.ts:222`), and the refund request CAS makes a second request for the same payment impossible. |
32:
33:## Consequences the design must respect
34:
35:- **The endpoint may request a refund, never execute one.** Settlement stays admin-only.
36:- **No new schema.** `is_paid`, `refund_status` and `payment_refunds` already carry everything.
37:- **The refund amount must come from the policy helper**, never from the client or a
38:  hand-rolled calculation.
39:- **Ownership is `TournamentAccessService.isManager`**, matching every other participant
40:  mutation, not an organization column.
41:
42:## Out of scope
43:
44:- Changing who can settle refunds.
45:- Partial refunds — the existing API cannot express one.
46:- Any change to the payment capture path.

