[web/changes/organizer-fee-paid-checkbox-20261005/03-endpoint-contract.md#950B]
1:# Endpoint Contract - organizer-fee-paid-checkbox-20261005
2:
3:## Added
4:
5:### `PATCH /tournaments/:id/participants/:participantId/fee-payment`
6:
7:Path params `:id` and `:participantId` are UUIDs. Role: `ORGANIZER` or `ADMIN`,
8:plus the global JWT guard and `Verified`.
9:
10:Request body — `UpdateParticipantFeePaymentDto`:
11:
12:```json
13:{ "paid": true }
14:```
15:
16:`paid` is required and must be a boolean.
17:
18:Response — `ApiResponse<...>`:
19:
20:```json
21:{
22:  "participant": { "...": "TournamentParticipant" },
23:  "refundRequested": false,
24:  "refundPaymentId": null
25:}
26:```
27:
28:| Field | Meaning |
29:|---|---|
30:| `refundRequested` | this call created a new `PENDING_REFUND` request |
31:| `refundPaymentId` | the payment that request was raised against, else `null` |
32:
33:`refundRequested` is `false` when the payment already carried a refund state, even
34:though a completed payment was found. It reports what this call did, not what exists.
35:
36:### Status codes
37:
38:| Code | When |
39:|---|---|
40:| 200 | applied, or a no-op because the flag already matched |
41:| 400 | validation failed on the body |
42:| 401 / 403 | not authenticated, or not a manager of this tournament |
43:| 404 | tournament missing, or the participant belongs to another tournament |
44:| 409 | a concurrent request already raised the refund for this payment |
45:
46:## Unchanged
47:
48:Every existing endpoint is untouched, including `PATCH :id/participants/:participantId`,
49:`:id/kick`, `:id/withdraw` and `POST /payments/admin/payments/:id/confirm-refund`.
50:Their routes, bodies and semantics are identical before and after.
51:
52:## Client binding
53:
54:`features/tournaments/api.ts` gains `setParticipantFeePaid(id, participantId, paid)`
55:returning the payload above. It is a new method on an existing client object; no
56:other client signature moves, and no other consumer of these types changes.
57:
58:## Compatibility
59:
60:- No database change, so no migration ordering to coordinate.
61:- Older deployed frontends are unaffected: they simply do not call the new route.
62:- The response reuses the existing `TournamentParticipant` shape, so nothing new has
63:  to be taught to older readers.

